The way a model reply is set in src/tui.c follows the scrollback in Grok Build
(https://github.com/xai-org/grok-build): headings, strong text, lists, quotes,
and fenced code are styled, and the markdown marks are not shown. Grok Build
is Copyright 2023-2026 SpaceXAI and is released under the Apache License,
Version 2.0 (http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0). beige does not
include Grok Build source. The renderer in src/tui.c is beige's own code.

No source from Pi (https://pi.dev) or Claude Code is included. The tool list
follows Pi's small loop (read, edit, write, and a shell). Ask, plan, and auto
follow the permission modes used by OpenCode and Claude Code. A user turn is
marked with `>`, which is the mark Claude Code uses for the user's text.
